# Changes under .github/ (workflows, the gate and sweep scripts, this file,
# Dependabot config) need the repo owner's review. The identifier-sweep
# workflow runs with a secret on main, so whoever can change .github/ can
# reach that secret; this rule (with branch protection requiring code-owner
# review) keeps that to the owner. GitHub reads it from the base branch, so a
# pull request cannot remove its own reviewer.
/.github/ @caseycapshaw
# .gitattributes can hide content from grep (e.g. working-tree-encoding).
/.gitattributes @caseycapshaw
